# Bio content seam

This repo is the S3 Biology site inside a UniPlus iframe. Teachers may add and rewrite teaching content freely. Platform wiring stays frozen.

## Do this

Edit the smallest content file that already holds that kind of material (quiz data, notes, flashcards, CSS, captions, images, browser-only tools).

Quiz content files only:

- Ch 2: `public/osmosis/js/cellQuizData.js`, `cellQuizExercises.js`
- Ch 3: `public/osmosis/js/membraneQuizData.js`, `membraneQuizExercises.js`
- Ch 4: `public/osmosis/js/enzymeQuizData.js`, `enzymeQuizExercises.js`
- Ch 5: `public/osmosis/js/foodNutritionQuizData.js`, `foodNutritionQuizExercises.js`
- Hub counts: `public/osmosis/quiz-hub.html`

New questions get new `id` values. Old `id` values stay. Match `section` to an id in `QUIZ_SECTIONS`.

## Stop and ask the technical owner if the task needs

`public/osmosis/js/*Quiz.js` (the runners), `*QuizUtils.js`, `*QuizExport.js`, `*QuizEffects.js`, `*QuizSummary.js`, `uni-tracker.js`, `postMessage`, `uniplus:*` payloads, `functions/`, `.github/`, Supabase, `fetch` / XHR, `uniplus_session`, or a new quiz data format.

## Before finishing

Run `node --check` on every edited `.js` file (CI skips `public/`). If a forbidden file is in the diff, revert it. Do not push.
